course: dictionary
lesson: 4770
title: How: the many jobs of one small word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word how asks about the way something happens or is done. «How do you make a kite?» does not want yes or no. It asks for the method, so the answer tells you the steps.
explain: Look at the word after how to find its job. With many or much, how asks about an amount: «how many apples» wants a number, and «how much water» wants a quantity. With an adjective like old, tall or far, how asks about age, height or distance.
explain: How can also join two parts of a sentence without asking a question. «I know how to swim» means I know the way to swim. To check, swap in the way: I know the way to swim. It still makes sense, so how means the way there.
fact: How asks in what way something happens: «How do you make a kite?»
fact: With «many» or «much», how asks about an amount: «how many apples», «how much water».
fact: With an adjective, how asks about size, age or distance: «how old», «how tall», «how far».
fact: How can ask about feelings or health: «How are you?»
fact: In «I know how to swim», how joins two parts of a sentence and means the way to do something.
exercise: «How do you make a kite?» What is this question asking about? | The colour of the kite | The number of kites | The name of the shop | *The way to make a kite
exercise: Which words ask about an amount in «telling her how much is left»? | Keep the change | Honest gift | *How much | Gran says
exercise: Which sentence uses how to ask about age or size? | «Keep the change, Gran.» | *«How tall is the giraffe?» | «Good morning, class.» | «I know the way to swim.»
test: In «To find how many there were at the start, begin at the end», what does how many ask for? | The name of the people | *A number | A feeling | The way to start
test: Which sentence uses how to ask about feelings or health? | «How far is the shop?» | *«How are you feeling today?» | «How tall is the tree?» | «How do you make a kite?»
exam: In a formal exam, which phrase replaces «how many»? | Once upon a time | Keep the change | Good morning, class | *Determine the number of
